           self.lines_filter,
           self.prepend_filter,
           self.append_filter,
           self.dedent_filter]
```

So prepend/append are inserted BEFORE dedent is applied. We need to change the order so dedent is applied to the file content (after filtering by pyobject/start/end/lines), and THEN prepend/append are inserted.

But wait — there's a subtlety. If we move prepend/append AFTER dedent, then dedent will only apply to the actual file content. But what about lineno-match? Let me check.

Actually, the cleanest fix per the issue: "Use of dedent could be a good solution, if dedent was applied only to the literalinclude and not to the prepend and append content."

So we should change the filter order to:
```python
filters = [self.pyobject_filter,
           self.start_filter,
           self.end_filter,
           self.lines_filter,
           self.dedent_filter,
           self.prepend_filter,
           self.append_filter]
```

This way dedent applies only to the file content, and then prepend/append are inserted at the end (without being dedented).

