All relevant tests pass. The patch is complete:

1. Fixed `sphinx/util/rst.py`: changed `docinfo_re` regex from `':\\w+:.*?'` to `r':\w+:(?:\s+.*)?$'` so that domain-directive headings like `:mod:\`mypackage2\`` are not mistaken for docinfo fields.
2. Added a regression test in `tests/test_util_rst.py`.

The root cause: `prepend_prolog` scans the beginning of the document for docinfo fields (lines matching `:\w+:`). The old regex matched any line starting with `:word:` — including section titles that contain a domain directive such as `:mod:\`mypackage2\``. Since it matched, `prepend_prolog` inserted a blank line *after* the first line, separating the title from its underline (`===`), which broke the heading. The new regex requires that after the field name colon there is either whitespace (field body) or end-of-line, which is how real docinfo fields look; `:mod:\`...\`` has a backtick after the colon, so it's no longer treated as docinfo.

