The patch is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what was done:

## Changes

**`sphinx/builders/linkcheck.py`** (the actual bug fix):
1. Imported `TooManyRedirects` from `requests.exceptions`
2. Changed the inner `except HTTPError:` clause to `except (HTTPError, TooManyRedirects):` so that when a HEAD request fails with an infinite redirect loop (`TooManyRedirects`), the linkchecker falls back to a GET request instead of immediately reporting the link as broken.

**`tests/test_build_linkcheck.py`** (regression test):
- Added `test_follows_redirects_on_GET_with_HEAD_redirect_loop` which serves a URL whose HEAD handler always redirects to itself (triggering `TooManyRedirects`) but whose GET handler works normally. It verifies the link is not reported as broken.

## Verification
All three related tests pass:
```
tests/test_build_linkcheck.py::test_follows_redirects_on_HEAD
tests/test_build_linkcheck.py::test_follows_redirects_on_GET
tests/test_build_linkcheck.py::test_follows_redirects_on_GET_with_HEAD_redirect_loop
3 passed
```

(Note: the default `python` in this environment is 3.14 where `imghdr` was removed, so tests were run with the `mas` conda env's Python 3.11

