All test cases pass, including the new one. The fix is complete:

1. **`visit_Tuple`** in `sphinx/pycode/ast.py` now appends a trailing comma when the tuple has exactly one element, so `(1,)` unparses as `(1,)` instead of `(1)`.

2. **`visit_Subscript`** was also fixed for consistency: a single-element tuple used as a subscript (e.g. `x[1,]` / `Tuple[(1,)]`) now preserves the trailing comma in the `[...]` slice.

3. Added the test case `("(1,)", "(1,)")` to `tests/test_pycode_ast.py` as described in the bug report.

The pytest suite couldn't run in this environment due to an unrelated Python 3.14 compatibility issue with plugin import (`sphinx.testing.fixtures`), so I verified by directly exercising the unparse function with all the parametrized cases — all 19 pass

